---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const feedUrl = new URL('/rss.xml', Astro.site).href;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="RSS feed — Qingze Luo"
  description="What RSS is and how to subscribe to Qingze Luo's writing."
>
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Subscribe</p>
    <h1>RSS feed</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      A small, open format for following new posts without an inbox.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap prose feed-body">
    <h2>What is RSS?</h2>
    <p>
      RSS is a standard feed format. The site publishes a machine-readable list of new posts at
      <code>/rss.xml</code>; a feed reader checks that file and shows new writing when it appears.
    </p>
    <p>
      Browsers often show the feed as raw XML. That is normal: the file is meant for a feed
      reader, not for reading in a browser tab.
    </p>

    <h2>How to subscribe</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Copy the feed URL: <code>{feedUrl}</code></li>
      <li>Add it to a feed reader such as Feedly, NetNewsWire, Reeder, or Inoreader.</li>
      <li>New posts will appear there automatically.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Feed URL</h2>
    <p>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/rss.xml">Open the raw RSS feed ↗</a>
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      If you do not use a feed reader, you can ignore this page; the blog is also available at
      <a href="/blog/">/blog/</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .feed-body {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin-inline: 0;
    padding-bottom: 80px;
  }
</style>
